# SwiftData

- Prefer SwiftData over Core Data unless a required feature is unavailable.
- Use `@Query` only inside SwiftUI views; outside views, use `ModelContext` and `FetchDescriptor`.
- Make relationships explicit when behavior matters, including inverse and delete rules.
- Keep predicates within supported SwiftData operations and avoid known runtime crash patterns.
- Consider indexing, CloudKit constraints, and model inheritance only when the deployment target and feature set require them.
- Favor clarity and correctness of the data model over clever query shortcuts.
